#callout(kind: "remember")[
  A *past tense verb* tells us about something that already happened. Most verbs add _-ed_: walk → walk*ed*. Some verbs change completely: go → went.
]

= Part A: Fill in the blanks

Write the past tense of the verb in brackets.

#question(points: 1)[
  Yesterday, we #blank(answer: [played]) football in the park. (play)
]

#question(points: 1)[
  She #blank(answer: [walked]) to school last Monday. (walk)
]

#question(points: 1)[
  The children #blank(answer: [ate]) lunch at noon. (eat)
]

#question(points: 1)[
  My dad #blank(answer: [went]) to the market this morning. (go)
]

#question(points: 1)[
  I #blank(answer: [saw]) a rainbow after the rain. (see)
]

#question(points: 1)[
  Tom #blank(answer: [jumped]) over the puddle. (jump)
]

= Part B: Matching

#question(points: 5)[
  Match each present tense verb to its past tense.
  #matching(
    ([run], [ran]),
    ([swim], [swam]),
    ([write], [wrote]),
    ([bring], [brought]),
    ([drink], [drank]),
  )
]

= Part C: Choose the correct word

#question(points: 1)[
  Which sentence is correct?
  #mcq([He goed to the zoo.], [He went to the zoo.], [He gone to the zoo.], answer: 2)
]

#question(points: 2)[
  #true-false(answer: true)[The past tense of _look_ is _looked_.]
  #true-false(answer: false)[The past tense of _sing_ is _singed_.]
]

= Part D: Writing task

#question(points: 5)[
  Write 4 or 5 sentences about what you did last weekend. Use at least *three* past tense verbs. Underline each past tense verb you use.
  #answer-lines(count: 5, spacing: 2.2em, answer: [Sample answer: On Saturday I visited my grandmother. We cooked rice together and then played a board game. On Sunday I helped my mum and watched a film.])
]

